UPSTREAM RELEASES UNDER stock/

Each package's stock/ directory carries the upstream project at a pinned
release, under that project's own licence: the release archive or wheel as
published (apart from the exceptions listed below) and, in most packages, an
unpacked reading copy of it or of the upstream repository at the pinned commit
(stock/src/). The package's LICENSE file names the upstream licence, whose
text travels inside stock/ and under the package's third_party_licenses/.
Beside the upstream files every stock/ directory holds two files written for
this tree, PINS.json (versions and SHA-256 pins) and check_pins.py; some also
hold this tree's install helpers and patch files
(af3_jax/stock/unpack_src.sh and stock/patches/,
af3_torch/stock/fetch_upstream.py and stock/patches/,
openfold3_ob0/stock/install_upstream.py), the PyPI metadata and provenance
records of the pinned wheel (opendde/stock/pypi_*.json), the
model card and configuration of the pinned checkpoint (enformer/stock/snapshot/,
from the model repository named in enformer/STOCK.md) and, in e1, the Hugging
Face hub kernel that stock E1 loads (e1/stock/hub_kernel/: the kernel's files
and their BSD-3-Clause LICENSE, plus SOURCE.md written for this tree).

The upstream files under stock/ are byte-identical to the pinned releases with
these exceptions, each declared in the package's STOCK.md:
  - af3_jax: stock/src/src/alphafold3/model/network/template_modules.py
    carries the package's one declared bug-fix patch (nine added lines); the
    archive stock/alphafold3-bc32b22f.tar.gz is unmodified.
  - pxdesign: the PXDesign reading copy and archive leave out two font files
    of upstream's pxdesign/pxd_server/ directory (Helvetica-Regular.ttf,
    TimesNewRoman.ttf: proprietary typefaces of Linotype and Monotype that
    upstream bundles for its server page), which nothing in the package
    reads (pxdesign/STOCK.md).
  - colabdesign: the BindCraft reading copy and archive leave out the two
    pre-compiled third-party executables upstream bundles under functions/:
    dssp, which run.sh install fetches from the BindCraft repository at the
    pinned commit and verifies by digest, and DAlphaBall.gcc, which is not
    distributed, not fetched and not used by any route of the package
    (colabdesign/STOCK.md, colabdesign/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
  - complexa: the Proteina-Complexa archive leaves out one member,
    src/proteinfoundation/result_analysis/sc, a pre-compiled third-party
    executable that upstream's README says is obtained separately; nothing
    the package runs reads it (complexa/STOCK.md 'Stock exceptions').
PXDesignBench is not carried in this tree; pxdesign's run.sh install fetches it
from upstream at its pinned commit, under its own licence.

