PROFLUENT-E1 (package e1)

e1 builds on Profluent-E1 (Profluent Bio Inc.), which is distributed under the
Profluent-E1 Clickthrough License Agreement together with the Profluent-E1
Attribution Guidelines; copies exactly as released are e1/stock/src/LICENSE,
e1/stock/src/NOTICE and e1/stock/src/ATTRIBUTION. Recipients of e1 receive
Profluent-E1 under that Agreement; downloading or using Profluent-E1 is
acceptance of it. The Agreement and Guidelines require attribution to
"Profluent-E1" in distributions and documentation and, for redistribution in
object form, a display of "Profluent-E1" each time the resulting program runs:
e1/README.md carries the statement "This project builds upon Profluent-E1 under
the terms of the Profluent-E1 Clickthrough License Agreement", and e1/run.sh
prints a one-line Profluent-E1 attribution naming the Agreement file at the
start of every command. The Profluent-E1 model weights are not carried; e1's
run.sh install --weights fetches them from the provider.

MODEL WEIGHTS

No package distributes the weights of the model it wraps, in this tree or in
images built from it; users obtain them from the original providers under
those providers' terms, and each package's STOCK.md names the source and the
terms. Small parameter files that upstream projects ship inside their own
source releases travel inside the carried archives exactly as released:
colabdesign (ColabDesign archive: eight ProteinMPNN parameter files, MIT, and
colabdesign/af/weights/template_dgram_head.npy, a small parameter array
ColabDesign ships for AlphaFold 2's template distogram head; AlphaFold 2
parameters are CC BY 4.0, DeepMind), mosaic (ProteinMPNN and AbMPNN weight
files, MIT and CC BY 4.0, and a CC BY 4.0 trigram table), borzoi (Baskerville
archive: tests/data/eval/model.h5, a small trained test model released with
Baskerville, Apache-2.0) and enformer (enformer-pytorch's
precomputed/tf_gammas.pt, a table of positional constants, MIT). They are
listed in those packages' THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md files.

DATA FILES IN CARRIED RELEASES AND IN THE PACKAGES

Several upstream releases ship example or test data drawn from public sequence
and structure databases; those files travel inside the carried archives and
reading copies exactly as released, under the databases' own terms:
  - rosettafold3: foundry archive member
    models/rf3/docs/examples/msas/3en2_A.a3m.gz, an alignment of UniRef100
    sequences (UniProt Consortium, CC BY 4.0); rfdiffusion3's foundry archive
    carries the rfd3 documentation's example input structures (wwPDB-derived).
  - pxdesign: stock/src/PXDesign/examples/ (also inside the archive): the PDL1
    example alignments pairing.a3m and non_pairing.a3m hold UniRef100,
    UniProtKB and UniParc sequences (CC BY 4.0), MGnify protein sequences
    (EMBL-EBI: CC0 1.0, releases before 2019 CC BY 4.0) and sequences of the
    ColabFold environmental database, which is built from BFD, MGnify and
    metagenome assemblies (CC BY-SA 4.0); 5o45.cif is a wwPDB entry.
  - openfold3, openfold3_ob0: stock/src/openfold3/tests/test_data/ holds
    upstream's test alignments for PDB entry 2Q2K (hits drawn from UniRef90 and
    UniProtKB, CC BY 4.0; MGnify, CC0 1.0 or CC BY 4.0 by release; BFD and
    Uniclust30, CC BY-SA 4.0; and template searches against PDB chain
    sequences), wwPDB mmCIF files and the NumPy/pickle snapshots produced by
    upstream's tests.
  - esm_if1: the fair-esm archive's examples/ hold alignments built from
    UniRef (CC BY 4.0) and from Uniclust30 (hhblits_uniclust_2017_10_*.a3m;
    Uniclust, CC BY-SA 4.0), the TEM-1 beta-lactamase mutational-scanning
    data of the variant-prediction example (BLAT_ECOLX_Ranganathan2015*.csv,
    P62593.fasta, as released with fair-esm), wwPDB coordinate files (4UV3,
    5YH2, 2N2U) and the lm-design example data.
  - af3_jax: the AlphaFold 3 archive's src/alphafold3/test_data/ holds
    miniature_databases/ — small excerpts that upstream includes for its
    tests, with the terms upstream states for them in
    af3_jax/stock/src/README.md: BFD (Steinegger and Söding, CC BY-SA 4.0;
    the excerpt as modified by Google DeepMind is stated there as CC BY 4.0),
    MGnify, PDB mmCIF and seqres, Rfam and RNAcentral (CC0 1.0), UniProt and
    UniRef90 (CC BY 4.0) and NCBI NT (NCBI's terms) — and upstream's
    featurised example and stored model outputs (*.pkl, *.json) generated
    from them.
  - esmc, esmfold2: the esm archive's esm/data/ holds entry, hierarchy and
    keyword tables derived from InterPro (EMBL-EBI, CC0 1.0) as released with
    esm.
  - complexa and genie3: the target structure sets of Proteina-Complexa
    (assets/target_data/) and of Genie's binder benchmark
    (data/design/binder_design/binderbench/) are crops, excerpts or prepared
    models of wwPDB entries and published de novo binder targets as released by
    those projects (Proteina-Complexa states CC BY 4.0 for its prepared data in
    licenses/license_datasets.txt inside the archive); af2ig's dl_binder_design
    archive carries its examples/ (wwPDB-derived target crops with the authors'
    designed binder models) and the AlphaFold 2 test structures it vendors;
    colabdesign's BindCraft copy carries example/PDL1.pdb (a crop of a
    deposited PD-L1 structure); chrombpnet's archive carries the motif tables
    of its data/ directory (position-weight matrices compiled by upstream from
    JASPAR, CC BY 4.0, and HOCOMOCO, with upstream's own bias motifs); borzoi's
    archives carry Borzoi's data/ tables and Baskerville's tests/data/
    (including hg38_1m.fa.gz, a one-megabase excerpt of the GRCh38 human
    reference assembly, and miniature training shards); opendde's reading copy
    carries examples/2lwu.cif and 7pzb.pdb (wwPDB entries); flashzoi's wheel
    carries Borzoi's track table (precomputed/targets.txt) and gpnstar's
    archive a 128-bp alignment fixture of the store named below.
wwPDB archive data are free of all copyright restrictions (CC0 1.0).

Test and example inputs written into the packages themselves (tests/inputs,
public_inputs, inputs_public, inputs/msa, inputs/targets, tests/specs,
tests/fixtures and examples directories) are public records or synthetic:
coordinate files are wwPDB entries or crops of them, named by their PDB
identifiers, with two exceptions — boltzgen's PD-L1 test specification
(opt/forward/fast_inference/tests/specs/PDL1_IgV_Q9NZQ7_18-132.pdb) is a
trimmed AlphaFold Protein Structure Database model (AF-Q9NZQ7-F1; CC BY 4.0,
DeepMind and EMBL-EBI), and rfdiffusion1's inputs_public/insulin_target.pdb is
a computed structure model (its header reads EXPDTA THEORETICAL MODEL) — the
insulin receptor target example distributed with RFdiffusion (BSD-3-Clause) —
not a wwPDB entry. Test sequences are those entries' sequences or synthetic
(e1's warm-up set); the alignment files (.a3m) in these directories are single-
sequence (query-only) inputs and contain no database sequences; flashzoi's
warm-up window (opt/forward/kits_v1_25/canary_window_0.npz) is a one-hot
524,288-bp window of the GRCh38 human reference assembly; gpnstar's
examples/msa/ is a 0.14-MiB excerpt of the public 100-vertebrate alignment
store described in gpnstar/examples/README.md (Hugging Face dataset
songlab/multiz100way, dataset card licence MIT; alignment origin UCSC hg38
multiz100way). Where a directory needs entry-level attribution it or its parent
carries a README, NOTICE, PROVENANCE or SOURCES file.

COPYLEFT AND SHARE-ALIKE TERMS INSIDE CARRIED RELEASES

Two kinds of file with copyleft or share-alike terms travel inside carried
releases exactly as their upstream projects ship them, unmodified.
OpenStructure's stereo_chemical_props.txt data table (LGPL-3.0), the file
AlphaFold 2 and OpenFold obtain from OpenStructure, travels in four byte-
identical copies: in colabfold's two wheels (colabfold-1.6.1, member
colabfold/openstructure/ with the LGPL text beside it;
alphafold_colabfold-2.3.13, member alphafold/common/), in af2ig's
dl_binder_design archive (member af2_initial_guess/alphafold/common/) and in
complexa's Proteina-Complexa archive (member
community_models/openfold/resources/); colabfold/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
describes the file and its licence. The alignment data drawn from BFD,
Uniclust30 or the ColabFold metagenomic sets named above (esm_if1's Uniclust30
alignment, the bfd_uniclust_hits.a3m files of openfold3 and openfold3_ob0, the
environmental-database entries of pxdesign's non_pairing.a3m) are under CC BY-
SA 4.0. No other GPL- family licence applies to a file in this tree or inside
the carried archives.
